# Line endings.
#
# The batch files are CRLF-only as far as cmd.exe is concerned: with LF-only
# endings cmd mis-parses blocks and can drop the last line.  Normalise them to
# LF in the repository (so diffs stay readable) but always check them out as
# CRLF, whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine doing the clone.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Everything else: normalise on commit, native endings on checkout.
* text=auto

# Keep the release binaries and the generated bundle out of diffs.
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.js binary

# ...except the bundle's source, which is hand-written text and should diff
# (the *.js binary rule above is for the generated bundles in data/ and fonts/;
# it expands to -diff -merge -text, so all three have to be undone here).
src/*.js text diff merge

# ...and the platform's own JavaScript, for the same reason.  What it is
# written in is the point of veusz-js-engine: jsapi.js is the API a feature is
# written against, and features/*/feature.js is a feature.  They are 11 KiB and
# a few KiB of reviewable code, and under the rule above neither showed a diff,
# so a change to a feature was invisible in git log -p.
#
# Still binary, deliberately: the generated MathJax bundle (features/mathjax/
# mathjax.js, 6.3 MB), the twenty font data files beside it, and katex.min.js,
# which is a third-party build.
veusz-js-engine/jsapi.js text diff merge
veusz-js-engine/features/*/feature.js text diff merge
